# SLASH — the AMD Alveo V80 runtime. https://github.com/Xilinx/SLASH
#
# FINN builds against this: MakeCPPDriver compiles finn-vrt-driver for the
# slash-vrt platform, ShellFlowType.SLASH_ALVEO is a supported shell flow, and
# post_synth_res.py parses SLASH synthesis reports.
#
# supply, not fetch. AMD publishes no SLASH packages; the repo carries Debian
# and RPM packaging, so you build the deb yourself. You already have it: SLASH
# needs a kernel module on the host, so anyone using a V80 has built and
# installed it there and the deb is a by-product.
#
#   git clone --recursive https://github.com/Xilinx/SLASH
#   # build per its README, then take the deb from packaging/
#   cp slash*.deb <finn>/docker/packages/slash.deb
#
# Host half: the SLASH kernel module and the vrtd daemon.
#
# UNVERIFIED: the userspace here and the host kernel module are probably
# version-coupled. If they are, using your own deb is not just cheaper than one
# FINN builds -- it is the only correct option. Confirm before you rely on it.
#
# SLASH needs Vivado 2025.1. build_dataflow_checks.py:81 asserts this for the
# SLASH_ALVEO flow. Vivado is a runtime mount, so docker/config.py resolves it and the
# check fires at build-config time, not here.
#
# No EXPECT_OS: you built this deb, so you know which release it targets. Set
# one if you want the image to check.
SOURCE=supply
FILES=slash.deb
